    "image_with_text_8LiFpr": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "eyebrow_yEinpp": {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "settings": {
            "text": "From Garden to Glass"
          }
        },
        "heading_qP8KfF": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "The Botanicals Behind Dunrobin Gin",
            "size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_hKhx4A": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>At the heart of Dunrobin Gin is a carefully balanced combination of juniper, coriander seed and angelica root, creating a classic gin foundation with a distinctive woodland character.</p><p>Lighter notes of lemon, rose-scented pelargonium and blackcurrant leaf add freshness and floral complexity, while a delicate touch of clove brings a gentle warmth to the finish.&nbsp;</p><p>Our rose-scented pelargonium is carefully grown in the formal gardens of Dunrobin Castle, where visitors can discover it for themselves, as well as near the Castle entrance, where it welcomes visitors on their arrival. Blackcurrant leaves are harvested from bushes in the Castle's kitchen gardens, nurtured by its experienced gardening team.&nbsp;</p><p>Once harvested, these botanicals are carefully preserved, steeped and infused, before being distilled using traditional copper pot stills crafted by Forsyths, renowned Scottish stillmakers based in Rothes, Speyside.</p><p>With generations of expertise in traditional copper craftsmanship, Forsyths are recognised for producing high-quality distillation equipment used by distilleries around the world. Their copper stills play an important role in the distillation process, helping to create a refined, balanced spirit that allows the carefully selected botanicals to shine through.</p><p>Combined with fresh spring water from the surrounding hills, every stage of production takes place on site at Dunrobin Highland Distillery, where founders Lizzie and Boban carefully craft their gin at Dunrobin Farm.</p><p>From garden to glass, the entire distilling process remains within the Golspie area, reflecting the Distillery's deep connection to its Highland home.</p><p>Together, these botanicals create a premium Scottish gin that captures the character of the gardens, woodland and natural beauty surrounding Dunrobin Castle.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "eyebrow_yEinpp",
