    "image_with_text_r4DrbB": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "eyebrow_WjKheA": {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Where we came from"
          }
        },
        "heading_etCrb7": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "The Story Behind Our Scottish Highland Gin",
            "size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_Mw46eQ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Creating the recipe for Dunrobin Gin was a collaborative labour of love, bringing together a shared passion for botanicals, the landscape and the heritage of Dunrobin Castle.</p><p>We were proud to work alongside two experts whose knowledge and creativity helped bring our vision to life.</p><p>Iain Crisp, Head Gardener at Dunrobin Castle, has spent 20 years tending the formal gardens and surrounding woodland. His extensive knowledge of the Castle's botanicals, and of the plants that thrive in this part of the Highlands, played an important role in developing the recipe.</p><p>We also worked closely with ethnobotanist&nbsp;<a href=\"https://susannemasters.com\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://susannemasters.com\">Susanne Masters</a>, whose expertise, creativity and understanding of the relationship between people and plants helped shape the final blend.</p><p>Together, their knowledge and guidance allowed us to create a gin that brings together the elements we felt were essential to representing Dunrobin Castle and its remarkable surroundings.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
